A||||5||Call||Question On A 1985 Fiero GT||||5||
Z||000000||Call||01-17-2000||12:34 PM||||Well I found a 1985 Fiero GT here at a dealer that has some side body damage and the engine is locked up, the dealer was asking 2500 originally but they said that they would come down. Im not quite sure how bad the side body damage is because I havent seen it yet and I have no clue what could be wrong with the engine. I might be able to bring them down really low because of this but what is all of your opinions on this car? I really like the 85' GTs and would love to get this one if the damage isn't too bad and the engine can be fixed fairly easily.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||01-17-2000||01:27 PM||||"Locked up" engine, body damage, dealer -- those words would scare me away from any deal other than "tow it away and it's yours" ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||01-17-2000||02:57 PM||||500.00 sounds too steep for that.  i don't care if they're worried about covering their costs of checking it out and cleaning it up.  you can find a better deal else where.  It just might take you a little while longer.||||reg||13
Z||000003||Call||01-17-2000||03:08 PM||||Well im going to try to bring them down to $300 for it, if they wont take it I wont buy it, I figure if I can get it for $300 ill just have the engine rebuilt and by the time im done with it it will have run me around $1300 or so anyways, im not going to keep the body panels on it anyways since im building a Ferrari 308 kit car on it, just as long as the frame is not damaged. I looked some of the same cars on the internet for $600-$1900 that were the same car that were in good condition and were running, I printed these out and when I go down there I am going to show them to the dealer to see if he will come down alot.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||01-18-2000||09:27 AM||||The interior would have to be in darn good shape, and the body damage would have to be minimal for it to be worth $300.  And they would have to deliver it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||01-18-2000||09:33 AM||||I usually pay a little more than Fieros are really worth, and even I think that's way too steep.  In the past year I've seen the following:<P>85 GT, clutch totally shot, motor started and sounded great, good body w/bad paint, $500<P>86 SE, clutch on the way out, trunk lock punched out, broken 1/4 windows, but ran good and had good paint, $900<P>86 GT, great body, paint and interior, engine totally disassembled, $1500<P>I had to pass on all of these.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
